ministrators Prospective Candidates Shortlisted Candidates Click to open inner submenu Interview Phase Information for New Academic Hires (Faculty,  Librarians, Chairs/Directors, Teaching/Research and Administrative) Click to open inner submenu Upon Hire Within Your First Two Weeks Within Your First Term Within Your First Year Frequently Asked Questions Postdoctoral Fellows Click to open inner submenu Become a Postdoctoral Fellow Hire, Appoint or Extend a Postdoctoral Fellow Postdoctoral Fellows Funding Options and Forms International Postdoctoral Fellows Health Insurance and Benefits Professional Development Opportunities News & Job Opportunities Postdoctoral Fellows FAQs Academic Labour Relations Click to open inner submenu Academic Labour Relations – Resources CUASA (Academic staff including faculty, instructors and professional librarians) CUPE 4600 Unit 1 (Teaching Assistants) CUPE 4600 Unit 2 (Contract Instructors) PSAC 77000 (Postdoctoral Fellows) Teaching Assistants Click to open inner submenu Getting Started TA Management System Contact Us Apply Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Continuing Studies Professional Development Programs Donate Carleton’s Commitment to Accessibility At Carleton, we strive to be a more inclusive, accessible community. This aspiration allows us to form deeper connections with one another as we work through stigma and barriers. We take accessibility into account from the start as we actively work to identify, address, and reduce barriers across the University community. We commit to a culture of accessibility to create an environment in which everyone has access and opportunity to fully participate and thrive in all aspects of campus life. About Accessibility at Carleton Accessibility and Wellness Events Resources Coordinated Accessibility Strategy Coordinated Accessibility Strategy Website Researchers in Accessibility Researchers in Accessibility Website Carleton University Disability Research Group Carleton University Disability Research Group Website PMC Resources for Faculty PMC Resources for Faculty Website Accessibility Resources Accessibility Resources Website Equity and Inclusion Resources Equity and Inclusion Resources Website Academic Positions Complete listing of Carleton’s full-time academic positions 613-520-2600 x7065 Email us Faculty, Staff, Librarians Academic Heads & Administrators Footer Carleton University acknowledges the location of its campus on the traditional, unceded territories of the Algonquin Anishinàbeg nation Admissions Undergraduate Graduate International Professional Development Financial Aid Campus Tours Initiatives Academics Schedules & Dates Brightspace Library Support Services Calendars Carleton Online Future Learning Lab Students Career Services Dept & Faculties Student Email Housing Registrar's Office Registration ITS Help Centre Campus Campus Map Directions Events Parking Safety Dining Services Clubs & Societies Ravens Giving to Carleton Athletics & Recreation GoRavens Varsity Contact us by phone or email 1125 Colonel By Drive, Ottawa, ON, K1S 5B6, Canada Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Policy Accessibility © Copyright\n                                2026 Search this website Submit This site uses cookies to offer you a better browsing experience. Find out more on how we use cookies and how you can change your settings. Ok, got it!"
