      "title": "Office of the AVP, Indigenous Teaching, Learning & Research",
      "description": "Carleton's Indigenous Academic Community - Office of the Deputy Provost Skip to Content Office of the Deputy Provost Apply Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Continuing Studies Professional Development Programs Donate Academic Jobs Click to open inner submenu Your Career at Carleton Current Academic Job Postings Contract Instructors Current Opportunities for American Scholars – Fulbright Visiting, In-Residence and Honorary Rank Appointments Faculty Affairs Click to open inner submenu Resources Faculty Affairs Top 10 for Academic Heads and Departmental Administrators Prospective Candidates Shortlisted Candidates Click to open inner submenu Interview Phase Information for New Academic Hires (Faculty,  Librarians, Chairs/Directors, Teaching/Research and Administrative) Click to open inner submenu Upon Hire Within Your First Two Weeks Within Your First Term Within Your First Year Frequently Asked Questions Postdoctoral Fellows Click to open inner submenu Become a Postdoctoral Fellow Hire, Appoint or Extend a Postdoctoral Fellow Postdoctoral Fellows Funding Options and Forms International Postdoctoral Fellows Health Insurance and Benefits Professional Development Opportunities News & Job Opportunities Postdoctoral Fellows FAQs Academic Labour Relations Click to open inner submenu Academic Labour Relations – Resources CUASA (Academic staff including faculty, instructors and professional librarians) CUPE 4600 Unit 1 (Teaching Assistants) CUPE 4600 Unit 2 (Contract Instructors) PSAC 77000 (Postdoctoral Fellows) Teaching Assistants Click to open inner submenu Getting Started TA Management System Contact Us Browse Academic Jobs Click to open inner submenu Your Career at Carleton Current Academic Job Postings Contract Instructors Current Opportunities for American Scholars – Fulbright Visiting, In-Residence and Honorary Rank Appointments Faculty Affairs Click to open inner submenu Resources Faculty Affairs Top 10 for Academic Heads and Departmental Administrators Prospective Candidates Shortlisted Candidates Click to open inner submenu Interview Phase Information for New Academic Hires (Faculty,  Librarians, Chairs/Directors, Teaching/Research and Administrative) Click to open inner submenu Upon Hire Within Your First Two Weeks Within Your First Term Within Your First Year Frequently Asked Questions Postdoctoral Fellows Click to open inner submenu Become a Postdoctoral Fellow Hire, Appoint or Extend a Postdoctoral Fellow Postdoctoral Fellows Funding Options and Forms International Postdoctoral Fellows Health Insurance and Benefits Professional Development Opportunities News & Job Opportunities Postdoctoral Fellows FAQs Academic Labour Relations Click to open inner submenu Academic Labour Relations – Resources CUASA (Academic staff including faculty, instructors and professional librarians) CUPE 4600 Unit 1 (Teaching Assistants) CUPE 4600 Unit 2 (Contract Instructors) PSAC 77000 (Postdoctoral Fellows) Teaching Assistants Click to open inner submenu Getting Started TA Management System Contact Us Apply Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Continuing Studies Professional Development Programs Donate Carleton’s Indigenous Academic Community Kinàmàgawin – Learning Together Located in Ottawa, Carleton University is situated within the unceded traditional territory of the Algonquin people and supports First Nations, Métis and Inuit students from across Canada. We recognize our special responsibility to support the recommendations of the Truth and Reconciliation Commission. We are working towards long-term change through the 41 calls to action articulated in Kinàmàgawin , our Indigenous initiatives strategy. As part of this, several full-time faculty positions have been created as a step toward reconciliation. We invite Indigenous candidates to join our team and help support Indigenous learners and bring Indigenous knowledge into classrooms. Indigenous Initiatives, News & Stories About Indigenous Faculty at Carleton Resources Professional Development Empowering educators with skills and knowledge to support Indigenous learners. More info Curricular Consultation Collaborating to integrate Indigenous perspectives into your curriculum. More info Student Support Consultations Personalized guidance to help Indigenous students thrive academically and personally. More info Centre for Indigenous Support and Community Engagement Building a supportive community for Indigenous students and fostering cultural connections. More info Office of the AVP, Indigenous Teaching, Learning & Research Leading initiatives to enhance Indigenous education and research at Carleton. More info Ānako Indigenous Research Institute Advancing Indigenous research and knowledge through collaborative projects and partnerships. More info Complete listing of Carleton’s full-time academic positions 613-520-2600 x7065 Email us Faculty, Staff, Librarians Academic Heads & Administrators Footer Carleton University acknowledges the location of its campus on the traditional, unceded territories of the Algonquin Anishinàbeg nation Admissions Undergraduate Graduate International Professional Development Financial Aid Campus Tours Initiatives Academics Schedules & Dates Brightspace Library Support Services Calendars Carleton Online Future Learning Lab Students Career Services Dept & Faculties Student Email Housing Registrar's Office Registration ITS Help Centre Campus Campus Map Directions Events Parking Safety Dining Services Clubs & Societies Ravens Giving to Carleton Athletics & Recreation GoRavens Varsity Contact us by phone or email 1125 Colonel By Drive, Ottawa, ON, K1S 5B6, Canada Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Privacy Policy Accessibility © Copyright\n                                2026 Search this website Submit This site uses cookies to offer you a better browsing experience. Find out more on how we use cookies and how you can change your settings. Ok, got it!"
